<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-slides – Vscode</title><link>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/tags/vscode/</link><description>Recent content in Vscode on go-slides</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/tags/vscode/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>VS Code</title><link>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/vscode/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/vscode/</guid><description>
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-blue-200 hx:bg-blue-100 hx:text-blue-900 hx:dark:border-blue-200/30 hx:dark:bg-blue-900/30 hx:dark:text-blue-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;The extension is &lt;a href="https://github.com/go-slides/vscode" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-slides/vscode&lt;/a&gt;,
versioned on its own (v0.2.2). It renders with go-slides v0.7.1 (the
&lt;code&gt;editor&lt;/code&gt; package, and the source lines of scroll sync). It is installed from
the &lt;code&gt;go-slides-0.2.2.vsix&lt;/code&gt; attached to its GitHub release: it is not on the VS
Code Marketplace or Open VSX yet.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The extension is go-slides&amp;rsquo; counterpart of
&lt;a href="https://github.com/marp-team/marp-vscode" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Marp for VS Code&lt;/a&gt;: the deck shows in
VS Code&amp;rsquo;s Markdown preview as slides, its errors in the Problems panel, and
directives, kinds and template functions complete as you type.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="install"&gt;Install&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="install"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#install" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download &lt;code&gt;go-slides-&amp;lt;version&amp;gt;.vsix&lt;/code&gt; from the
&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-slides/vscode/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;releases&lt;/a&gt;, then run
&lt;em&gt;Extensions: Install from VSIX&amp;hellip;&lt;/em&gt;, or:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;code --install-extension go-slides-0.2.2.vsix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The preview needs nothing else. Exporting needs the &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;go install github.com/go-slides/slides/cmd/slides@latest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="preview"&gt;Preview&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="preview"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#preview" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open a deck and &lt;em&gt;Markdown: Open Preview to the Side&lt;/em&gt;. A deck is a Markdown file
whose front matter says &lt;code&gt;slides: true&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nn"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;slides&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;paginate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;who&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;World&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nn"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="gh"&gt;# Hello {{ .who }}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;---
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- _kind: title --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;# Page {{ page }} of {{ total }}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Files with &lt;code&gt;marp: true&lt;/code&gt; are previewed too, unless Marp for VS Code is installed:
both extensions would render the same document. The setting
&lt;code&gt;goSlides.preview.marpDocuments&lt;/code&gt; decides: &lt;code&gt;auto&lt;/code&gt; (the default), &lt;code&gt;always&lt;/code&gt; or
&lt;code&gt;never&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The preview is go-slides itself, compiled to WebAssembly and loaded by the
extension: no binary, and it works on &lt;a href="https://vscode.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;vscode.dev&lt;/a&gt;. It reads
what the deck uses from the workspace — &lt;code&gt;slides.yaml&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;slides.hcl&lt;/code&gt; next to
the deck, the &lt;a href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/kinds/"&gt;kinds&lt;/a&gt; files they name, files a
&lt;a href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/templates/"&gt;template&lt;/a&gt; includes, theme CSS — and only from the
deck&amp;rsquo;s workspace folder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="scroll-sync"&gt;Scroll sync&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="scroll-sync"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#scroll-sync" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since v0.2.0 of the extension (go-slides v0.7.0), the editor and the
preview scroll together, both ways, as they do for plain Markdown: the
preview follows the slide and the block under the editor&amp;rsquo;s cursor, and
scrolling the preview moves the editor. The settings are VS Code&amp;rsquo;s own,
&lt;code&gt;markdown.preview.scrollPreviewWithEditor&lt;/code&gt; and
&lt;code&gt;markdown.preview.scrollEditorWithPreview&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lines are traced through templates. A slide that a &lt;code&gt;{{ range }}&lt;/code&gt; generates
follows the line of its template, and what an &lt;code&gt;{{ include }}&lt;/code&gt; brings in
follows the include&amp;rsquo;s line. A deck split by &lt;code&gt;headingDivider&lt;/code&gt; syncs on its
headings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="problems-completion-hover"&gt;Problems, completion, hover&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="problems-completion-hover"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#problems-completion-hover" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problems&lt;/strong&gt;: template, YAML and &lt;a href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/hcl/"&gt;HCL&lt;/a&gt; errors, on the
line they are on, in the deck or in the kinds file they come from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Completion&lt;/strong&gt;: directive keys in the front matter and in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;!-- --&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; comments
(with &lt;code&gt;_&lt;/code&gt; for a spot directive), the values of &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;_kind&lt;/code&gt; (with what
each kind sets), &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;size&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;paginate&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;math&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;headingDivider&lt;/code&gt;; inside
&lt;code&gt;{{ }}&lt;/code&gt;, the template functions and the data fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hover&lt;/strong&gt;: what a directive does, what a kind sets, a template function&amp;rsquo;s
arguments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="export"&gt;Export&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="export"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#export" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;go-slides: Export Slide Deck&amp;hellip;&lt;/em&gt; (also in the editor&amp;rsquo;s title bar) writes HTML,
vector PDF, editable PPTX and ODP, PNG or JPEG with the &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; command, as
&lt;code&gt;slides -o deck.pdf deck.md&lt;/code&gt; would; see &lt;a href="https://go-slides.github.io/docs/0.7/cli/"&gt;Command line&lt;/a&gt;.
It needs a trusted workspace. If &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; is not found, the extension offers to
run the &lt;code&gt;go install&lt;/code&gt; above in a terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="settings"&gt;Settings&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="settings"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#settings" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;goSlides.cliPath&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; command; empty: &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;. A machine setting: a workspace cannot set it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;goSlides.exportType&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;pdf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the format the export dialog proposes first&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;goSlides.exportAutoOpen&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;open the exported file&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;goSlides.html&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;allow all raw HTML instead of Marp&amp;rsquo;s allowlist; honoured only in a trusted workspace&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;goSlides.preview.marpDocuments&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;auto&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;preview &lt;code&gt;marp: true&lt;/code&gt; decks: &lt;code&gt;auto&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;always&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;never&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="security"&gt;Security&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="security"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#security" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The deck and the workspace are untrusted. Raw HTML follows Marp&amp;rsquo;s allowlist
unless &lt;code&gt;goSlides.html&lt;/code&gt; is on in a trusted workspace (a &lt;code&gt;slides.yaml&lt;/code&gt; with
&lt;code&gt;html: true&lt;/code&gt; does not turn it on in the preview), and VS Code&amp;rsquo;s preview runs no
script from the deck. The preview reads files of the deck&amp;rsquo;s workspace folder
only, follows no symbolic link, and templates see no environment variable.
Exporting runs a program, so it waits for workspace trust, and the program is
never named by the workspace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="performance"&gt;Performance&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="performance"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#performance" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;On go-slides&amp;rsquo; 100-slide benchmark deck, in VS Code 1.142 on an Apple M4 Max,
with Marp for VS Code 3.6.1 measured in the same session:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;go-slides&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Marp for VS Code&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;activation (loading the WebAssembly module)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;189 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;first preview&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;52 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;78 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;preview after an edit (median)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;24 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;23 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;.vsix&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;7.5 MB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;36.3 MB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The figures are for extension v0.2.2 (go-slides v0.7.1), from four interleaved
rounds under a 1-minute load of 5.9 to 7.5, at Go&amp;rsquo;s default &lt;code&gt;GOGC&lt;/code&gt;. The first
preview is faster than Marp&amp;rsquo;s, and the preview after an edit is level with
Marp&amp;rsquo;s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="in-v071-and-extension-v022"&gt;In v0.7.1 and extension v0.2.2&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="in-v071-and-extension-v022"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#in-v071-and-extension-v022" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;go-slides v0.7.1 caches parsed themes, packed style sheets and highlighted code
between renders, marks scroll-sync lines without going byte by byte, and reuses
its writers: a render of the 100-slide deck allocates 5.7 MB, against 52.7 MB
for extension v0.2.0. With it, extension v0.2.2 drops the &lt;code&gt;GOGC=400&lt;/code&gt; override.
For comparison, extension v0.2.1 took 72 ms for the first preview and 44 ms
after an edit at the default &lt;code&gt;GOGC&lt;/code&gt; (36 ms with &lt;code&gt;GOGC=400&lt;/code&gt;), and v0.2.0 took
47–51 ms.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>